title: End Reason
---

/*
  dsl 0.8.0 `::end`: the walk terminator. Both branch arms end the walk with
  their own `reason`, so the converge line below the <branch> is never
  reached on ANY route -- an engine that falls through to it (rather than
  stopping at the `end` record) fails this fixture on its very last command.

  The two `::end`s sit in DIFFERENT bodies, so neither makes the other's arm
  -- or the converge -- `W-CODE-AFTER-END` at check time: unreachability here
  is a whole-branch property, not a straight-line one.
*/

## The Parting

@narrator: The road ends at the river.

<branch id="parting">
  <choice id="stay" label="Hold the crossing">
    @hero: I'll hold the crossing.
    ::end{reason="stayed"}
  </choice>
  <choice id="leave" label="Walk away">
    @hero: There's nothing left here.
    ::end{reason="left"}
  </choice>
</branch>

@narrator: Never reached — both arms terminate the walk.
